>> title: Roasted Beet Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: beets, goat cheese, walnuts, orange, arugula
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: roasted beet salad, beet salad, beet and goat cheese salad, beetroot salad, beets and chevre, roasted beetroot salad
>> pairs-with: basic-vinaigrette
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — beets left an extra twenty minutes in the oven only get sweeter, and every part of this keeps three days apart
>> step.2: roast 400°F 1 hr
>> step.3: toast 6 min, cool hard
>> step.4: marinate 15 min
>> step.5: peel and quarter
>> step.6: arrange over the leaves

Preheat the #oven{} to 400°F (200°C).

Roast @beets{1 1/2%lb}(700 g; scrubbed, tops off) with @extra-virgin olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @thyme{4%sprigs} sealed in a foil parcel on a #sheet pan{} for ~roast{60%min}, until a knife slides to the middle.

Toast @walnuts{3/4%cup}(85 g) with @honey{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} in a #skillet{} over medium heat for ~toast{6%min}, then spread them out to ~cool{10%min}.

Marinate @goat cheese{4%oz}(115 g; broken in rough pieces) with @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @orange zest{1%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} for ~marinate{15%min}.

Peel @&(~3)roasted beets{} — the skins slip off under a thumb while they are warm — and quarter them.

Arrange @&(~1)quartered beets{}, @&(~2)marinated goat cheese{} and @&(~3)candied walnuts{} over @arugula{4%cups} with @orange segments{2}(cut free of their membranes) and @basic vinaigrette{1/4%cup}(60 mL).

Beets stain everything they are tossed with so this one is built rather than mixed and dressed last.
